# Memphis and Tulsa plan

From 2026-11-23, reroute 2,200 Memphis parcels a day to Tulsa.

data plan = depot,before,after; Memphis,104.0,100.0; Tulsa,94.3,99.5

chart bar plan x=depot unit=% target="100 capacity" labels title="Utilization before and after rerouting"

- **Memphis** drops to exactly 100.0% (55,000 parcels a day).
- **Tulsa** rises to 99.5% (41,800 of 42,000).
- Both depots run at their limit with no slack for the whole window.

cards

### Reroute to Tulsa (plan)
2,200 parcels a day from 2026-11-23. Leaves Tulsa with only 200 parcels a day of headroom.

### Omaha (fallback)
Could take up to 7,200 more parcels a day, but rerouting there adds a day of transit.

step All 640 seasonal workers start, 210 of them at Memphis | by 2026-11-16
step Reroute 2,200 Memphis parcels/day to Tulsa | 2026-11-23
step Peak window ends | 2026-12-23

# Risks

!! **No slack at Memphis or Tulsa.** Any outage or weather delay at either depot during the window has nowhere to go except Omaha, which adds a day of transit.

!! **Staffing dependency.** The plan relies on all 640 seasonal workers starting by 2026-11-16, including 210 at Memphis.
